cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "ai4fly-estimation: learned measurement models for joint state and sensor-health estimation"
abstract: >-
  Sensor health is carried as part of the filter state and a learned
  measurement model is conditioned on it, so that an unscented Kalman filter
  estimates vehicle state and per-sensor degradation jointly. The central
  result is that faults divide by which moment of the measurement
  distribution they disturb: mean-shifting faults are estimable through the
  health state, while variance-inflating faults are structurally invisible
  to it and require covariance matching. The two mechanisms are therefore
  complementary by construction, and the boundary between them is derivable
  from the measurement model before any experiment is run.
type: software
